# UI quality

- Follow `docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`; do not introduce a teal-led palette or decorative gradients.
- Use Manrope for display and DM Sans for interface copy; preserve the compact workspace density.
- Use Lucide icons, never emoji or text glyphs as interface icons.
- Borders communicate structure; avoid nesting every region in another rounded card.
- Keep controls at least 40px tall and provide visible `:focus-visible` states.
- Keep status meaning readable without color alone.
- At narrow widths, prefer a focused horizontal Kanban board over unusably narrow columns.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`; interaction motion must explain a state change.
- Use sentence case and specific actions: “Save task”, not “Submit”.
